      "Third, special wisdom for family cases. Jesus Himself faced this — His own brothers did not believe in Him during His ministry (John 7:5). Yet after the resurrection, His brother James became a leader of the Jerusalem church and wrote a New Testament letter. Family conversions often follow death, suffering, or a long-faithful life observed across decades. Do not panic. Do not push past listening. Do not let arguments end the relationship. Stay close, pray hard, and trust the Lord with timing.",
      "Finally, what to do when a long-prayed-for person dies without obvious faith. Grieve honestly. The Bible does not promise an answer to every soul's eternal state. But also remember: there are conversions in the final hours that no one witnesses but God. We do not know what passes between the soul and the Lord at the moment of death. Trust the Father, who is more merciful than your worst fears and more just than your best hopes. He has His ways.",
